        <section>
          <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9"/>
          <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Assessment and Plan"/>
          <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
          <text>
            <paragraph>72yo F presents with severe muscle pain, weakness, and dark urine (tea-colored). CK markedly elevated at 18,500 U/L. Creatinine 2.8 mg/dL (baseline 1.3) - acute kidney injury from rhabdomyolysis. Myoglobinuria present. Etiology: Drug-induced rhabdomyolysis from atorvastatin 80mg interacting with diltiazem (CYP3A4 inhibitor increases statin levels 3-4x). ATORVASTATIN DISCONTINUED. DILTIAZEM DISCONTINUED. Admitted for aggressive IV hydration to prevent ATN. Nephrology consulted. ACE inhibitor (lisinopril) held due to AKI. CRITICAL: Patient on triple antithrombotic therapy (warfarin + aspirin + clopidogrel) with declining renal function significantly increases bleeding risk.</paragraph>
          </text>
        </section>
